---
title: ProximaDB - Infrastructure & Bootstrap Subsystem
---
graph TB
    subgraph "Server Bootstrap"
        MAIN["Server Entry Point\napps/proximadb-server/src/main.rs\n- Parse CLI: config, data-dir, port\n- Load config from .toml files\n- Initialize logging + tracing\n- Start health server\n- Signal handling (SIGTERM/SIGINT)\n- Graceful shutdown orchestration"]
        CONFIG["Config Cascade\nsrc/config/ (6.5K LOC)\n- .env → profiles.yaml → CLI flags\n- TOML-based config structs\n- Hot-reload: SIGHUP → reload\n- Validated on startup\n- Environment variable interpolation"]
    end

    subgraph "Component Initialization"
        INIT["Initialization Sequence\n1. Config loaded\n2. Logging/tracing initialized\n3. ObjectStore connection verified\n4. Catalog bootstrapped (or created)\n5. WAL replayed (crash recovery)\n6. Storage engines initialized\n7. Indexes loaded (or built)\n8. Cluster join (if cluster mode)\n9. Network listeners bound\n10. Ready signal → /ready returns 200"]
    end

    subgraph "Infrastructure Services"
        HEALTH["Health Service\nsrc/infrastructure/\n- /health: liveness (always 200)\n- /ready: readiness (checks deps)\n- Dependency graph:\n  ✓ ObjectStore reachable\n  ✓ WAL recovered\n  ✓ Cluster connected (if clustered)\n  ✓ Catalog loaded\n- Graceful drain: /ready → 503\n  before shutdown"]
        SHUTDOWN["Graceful Shutdown\n- Drain: stop accepting new requests\n- Wait: inflight requests complete\n- Flush: WAL + memtable → disk\n- Close: storage engine, indexes\n- Signal: cluster peers (leave)\n- Exit: process exits cleanly"]
    end

    subgraph "Hardware Abstraction"
        HW["Hardware Detection\nproximadb-hardware / proximadb-hardware-caps\n- CPU: model, cores, AVX512/NEON\n- Memory: total RAM, NUMA topology\n- Disk: SSD vs HDD, IOPS, capacity\n- GPU: CUDA compute capability\n- Network: bandwidth, latency\n- Used for: engine auto-tuning,\n  thread pool sizing, SIMD dispatch"]
    end

    subgraph "Resource Pools"
        POOLS["Resource Pool Manager\nsrc/infrastructure/pools/\n- Thread pools:\n  * IO pool (tokio runtime)\n  * CPU pool (rayon)\n  * Flush pool (dedicated)\n  * Compaction pool (background)\n- Memory:\n  * Block cache budget\n  * Index memory budget\n  * WAL memtable budget\n- Connection pool:\n  * Object store connections\n  * gRPC channel pool"]
    end

    subgraph "Signal Handling"
        SIGNALS["Signal Handler\n- SIGTERM/SIGINT: graceful shutdown\n- SIGHUP: config reload\n- SIGUSR1: dump stats/debug info\n- SIGUSR2: rotate logs\n- Signal channel: tokio broadcast\n  to all components"]
    end

    MAIN --> CONFIG
    MAIN --> INIT
    INIT --> HEALTH
    INIT --> POOLS
    INIT --> HW

    HEALTH --> SHUTDOWN
    SIGNALS --> MAIN

    NETWORK["MultiServer\n(network init)"] --> INIT
    STORAGE["StorageEngine\n(storage init)"] --> INIT
    CLUSTER["ClusterService\n(cluster join)"] --> INIT

    classDef boot fill:#bbdefb,stroke:#1565c0
    classDef config fill:#c8e6c9,stroke:#2e7d32
    classDef init fill:#ffe0b2,stroke:#f57c00
    classDef infra fill:#e1bee7,stroke:#7b1fa2
    classDef hw fill:#ffcdd2,stroke:#d32f2f
    classDef pools fill:#b3e5fc,stroke:#0288d1
    classDef sig fill:#d7ccc8,stroke:#5d4037
    classDef ext fill:#b3e5fc,stroke:#0288d1,stroke-dasharray: 5 5

    class MAIN boot
    class CONFIG config
    class INIT init
    class HEALTH,SHUTDOWN infra
    class HW hw
    class POOLS pools
    class SIGNALS sig
    class NETWORK,STORAGE,CLUSTER ext
